slopmill is licensed in parts. Each part says which license it is under, and every source
file carries an SPDX line naming it.

  PART                                  LICENSE              TEXT
  The core: the compiler, the design    MIT                  LICENSES/MIT.txt
  and voice-pack file formats, and the
  library other programs can build on
  The slopmill application: the editor, AGPL-3.0-or-later    LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt
  its server, the model passes, the
  command-line program
  Voice packs (packs/*/voice/)          Each pack's own      packs/<name>/LICENSE.md
                                        LICENSE.md           LICENSES/VOICE-PACKS.md
  The name "slopmill" and its logo      Not licensed:        TRADEMARKS.md
                                        trademarks

Which files are which:

  MIT                slopmill/__init__.py, doc.py, source.py, render.py, pack.py,
                     pandoc.py, ids.py, errors.py, designs.py, voices.py;
                     packs/*/ (the designs; not their voice/ folders); docs/; tests/
  AGPL-3.0-or-later  slopmill/server/ (including the web editor in server/static/),
                     slopmill/agent.py, proof.py, export.py, providers.py, usage.py, setup.py,
                     cli.py, __main__.py

In short: build your own tools on the core and the file formats however you like. If you
change the slopmill application and let other people use your version, including over a
network, share your changes under the AGPL. Your own voice packs, designs and issues are
yours; slopmill claims nothing in them.

Copyright (c) 2026 byteclaw and the slopmill contributors.
